  date         = {2019},
  abstract     = {We develop a dynamic trade model with spatially distinct labor
                  markets facing varying exposure to international trade. The
                  model captures the role of labor mobility frictions, goods
                  mobility frictions, geographic factors, and input‐output
                  linkages in determining equilibrium allocations. We show how
                  to solve the equilibrium of the model and take the model to
